Your **borrowing power** is the maximum home loan amount an Australian lender will approve based on your income, expenses, and existing debts. Under APRA guidelines, all Australian lenders are required to assess your ability to repay the loan at your actual interest rate plus a **3% serviceability buffer** — so if the advertised rate is 6.3%, the bank tests your repayments at 9.3%. This buffer significantly reduces the loan amount you qualify for compared to what you might calculate at the advertised rate alone.

This calculator estimates your maximum borrowing capacity by deducting estimated income tax (using FY2025-26 ATO brackets) from your gross income, subtracting monthly living expenses and existing debt repayments, and calculating the loan size supportable at the buffered rate. The maximum property price shown assumes an 80% loan-to-value ratio (20% deposit), the standard threshold to avoid Lenders Mortgage Insurance (LMI). For a precise borrowing assessment, speak with a mortgage broker who can access lender-specific affordability calculators.
